Apply to stdlib/tui/render.nanz. NOT APPLIED: the guarded CP/M runtime admits
tui_read_key only by a byte-exact canonical body table in
minzc/pkg/mir2/cpm_runtime_tui_bodies.go, so any change to this asm is a
compiler change, and task Z1 forbids touching pkg/. With the patch applied
(and that table entry and the two freeze hashes below updated) every
unrecognised VT100 sequence is consumed and ignored instead of quitting the
caller; verified on a patched build:

    ESC [ 5 ~  (PageUp)          -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC [ H    (Home)            -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC [ 1 ~  (Insert)          -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC [ 3 ~  (Delete)          -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC [ Z    (Shift-Tab)       -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC O A    (SS3 up)          -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC Z      (DECID)           -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    ESC [ 1;5B (Ctrl-Down)       -> moved (ignored)  clears=2
    bare ESC                      -> no move (quit)   clears=2

("moved" means the `j` that follows the sequence still moved the cursor, so the
sequence was consumed rather than reported as ESC.)

To apply and verify:

    git apply --check reports/zvdb-demo-cpm/repro/tui_read_key-sequence-decode.patch
    git apply      reports/zvdb-demo-cpm/repro/tui_read_key-sequence-decode.patch
    minzc/mz examples/nanz/zvdb_demo_cpm.nanz -t cpm -o /tmp/zvdb.com
    printf '\033[5~jq' | minzc/mze /tmp/zvdb.com -t cpm --cpm-no-echo -c | tail -c 40

Three things to know before applying:
  * A "/" inside an asm block is a statement separator even inside a ";"
    comment. The original comment "then map A/B/C/D." assembled to three bogus
    instructions ("B", "C", "D.") and the assembler reported
    `unknown instruction or invalid operands: B`. Keep asm comments slash-free.
  * The canonical body must be updated in step with the asm, in
    minzc/pkg/mir2/cpm_runtime_tui_bodies.go, or every compile with
    Runtime: Z80RuntimeCPM fails with
    "CP/M runtime rejects ASM without canonical body: tui__render__tui_read_key"
    (seen in TestCPMTUIAdmissionAudit and TestCPMTetrisInvalidBoardStoreBeforeWrite).
  * stdlib/tui/render.nanz is pinned by SHA-256 in
    reports/tetris-main-native/freeze-corrected.json (dependency_sha256) and
    reports/tetris-family-native/freeze.json (sources). Both must be re-frozen
    together with the pkg/ table, or TestOriginalTetrisCPMMainNative and
    TestPublicCPMTetrisNative fail on the freeze rather than on the body.

diff --git a/stdlib/tui/render.nanz b/stdlib/tui/render.nanz
--- a/stdlib/tui/render.nanz
+++ b/stdlib/tui/render.nanz
@@ -255,7 +255,13 @@ fun tui_puts(str: ^u8) -> void {
 
